---
import './inventory-cash.css';
---

<figure class="not-prose" id="dd-payment-timing" aria-labelledby="buying-title" aria-describedby="example-assumptions">
      <div class="figure-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">A canned-tomato distributor’s buying decision</p>
        <h2 id="buying-title">One delivery.<br>Or one every week?</h2>
        <p class="setup">Customers need <strong>100 cases a week</strong> for the next four weeks. The supplier offers a <strong>$1-per-case discount</strong> if all 400 cases arrive at once.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="buying-plans">
        <section class="buying-plan bulk" aria-labelledby="bulk-title">
          <h3 id="bulk-title">Buy four weeks at once</h3>
          <p class="unit-price">$25 <span>per case</span></p>
          <p class="delivery-summary">400 cases in one delivery</p>
          <p class="chart-heading">Pallets stored during each week</p>
          <div class="stock-chart" role="img" aria-label="Pallets held during weeks 1 to 4: 8, 6, 4, 2."><div class="stock-week"><strong>8</strong><svg viewBox="0 0 72 104" aria-hidden="true"><g transform="translate(5 79)"><rect class="case" x="1" y="0" width="27" height="17" rx="1"/><path class="case-seam" d="M14.5 0v17M1 8.5h27"/><path class="pallet" d="M0 20h29M3 22v2m11.5-2v2M26 22v2"/></g><g transform="translate(38 79)"><rect class="case" x="1" y="0" width="27" height="17" rx="1"/><path class="case-seam" d="M14.5 0v17M1 8.5h27"/><path class="pallet" d="M0 20h29M3 22v2m11.5-2v2M26 22v2"/></g><g transform="translate(5 54)"><rect class="case" x="1" y="0" width="27" height="17" rx="1"/><path class="case-seam" d="M14.5 0v17M1 8.5h27"/><path class="pallet" d="M0 20h29M3 22v2m11.5-2v2M26 22v2"/></g><g transform="translate(38 54)"><rect class="case" x="1" y="0" width="27" height="17" rx="1"/><path class="case-seam" d="M14.5 0v17M1 8.5h27"/><path class="pallet" d="M0 20h29M3 22v2m11.5-2v2M26 22v2"/></g><g transform="translate(5 29)"><rect class="case" x="1" y="0" width="27" height="17" rx="1"/><path class="case-seam" d="M14.5 0v17M1 8.5h27"/><path class="pallet" d="M0 20h29M3 22v2m11.5-2v2M26 22v2"/></g><g transform="translate(38 29)"><rect class="case" x="1" y="0" width="27" height="17" rx="1"/><path class="case-seam" d="M14.5 0v17M1 8.5h27"/><path class="pallet" d="M0 20h29M3 22v2m11.5-2v2M26 22v2"/></g><g transform="translate(5 4)"><rect class="case" x="1" y="0" width="27" height="17" rx="1"/><path class="case-seam" d="M14.5 0v17M1 8.5h27"/><path class="pallet" d="M0 20h29M3 22v2m11.5-2v2M26 22v2"/></g><g transform="translate(38 4)"><rect class="case" x="1" y="0" width="27" height="17" rx="1"/><path class="case-seam" d="M14.5 0v17M1 8.5h27"/><path class="pallet" d="M0 20h29M3 22v2m11.5-2v2M26 22v2"/></g></svg><span>Week 1</span></div><div class="stock-week"><strong>6</strong><svg viewBox="0 0 72 104" aria-hidden="true"><g transform="translate(5 79)"><rect class="case" x="1" y="0" width="27" height="17" rx="1"/><path class="case-seam" d="M14.5 0v17M1 8.5h27"/><path class="pallet" d="M0 20h29M3 22v2m11.5-2v2M26 22v2"/></g><g transform="translate(38 79)"><rect class="case" x="1" y="0" width="27" height="17" rx="1"/><path class="case-seam" d="M14.5 0v17M1 8.5h27"/><path class="pallet" d="M0 20h29M3 22v2m11.5-2v2M26 22v2"/></g><g transform="translate(5 54)"><rect class="case" x="1" y="0" width="27" height="17" rx="1"/><path class="case-seam" d="M14.5 0v17M1 8.5h27"/><path class="pallet" d="M0 20h29M3 22v2m11.5-2v2M26 22v2"/></g><g transform="translate(38 54)"><rect class="case" x="1" y="0" width="27" height="17" rx="1"/><path class="case-seam" d="M14.5 0v17M1 8.5h27"/><path class="pallet" d="M0 20h29M3 22v2m11.5-2v2M26 22v2"/></g><g transform="translate(5 29)"><rect class="case" x="1" y="0" width="27" height="17" rx="1"/><path class="case-seam" d="M14.5 0v17M1 8.5h27"/><path class="pallet" d="M0 20h29M3 22v2m11.5-2v2M26 22v2"/></g><g transform="translate(38 29)"><rect class="case" x="1" y="0" width="27" height="17" rx="1"/><path class="case-seam" d="M14.5 0v17M1 8.5h27"/><path class="pallet" d="M0 20h29M3 22v2m11.5-2v2M26 22v2"/></g></svg><span>Week 2</span></div><div class="stock-week"><strong>4</strong><svg viewBox="0 0 72 104" aria-hidden="true"><g transform="translate(5 79)"><rect class="case" x="1" y="0" width="27" height="17" rx="1"/><path class="case-seam" d="M14.5 0v17M1 8.5h27"/><path class="pallet" d="M0 20h29M3 22v2m11.5-2v2M26 22v2"/></g><g transform="translate(38 79)"><rect class="case" x="1" y="0" width="27" height="17" rx="1"/><path class="case-seam" d="M14.5 0v17M1 8.5h27"/><path class="pallet" d="M0 20h29M3 22v2m11.5-2v2M26 22v2"/></g><g transform="translate(5 54)"><rect class="case" x="1" y="0" width="27" height="17" rx="1"/><path class="case-seam" d="M14.5 0v17M1 8.5h27"/><path class="pallet" d="M0 20h29M3 22v2m11.5-2v2M26 22v2"/></g><g transform="translate(38 54)"><rect class="case" x="1" y="0" width="27" height="17" rx="1"/><path class="case-seam" d="M14.5 0v17M1 8.5h27"/><path class="pallet" d="M0 20h29M3 22v2m11.5-2v2M26 22v2"/></g></svg><span>Week 3</span></div><div class="stock-week"><strong>2</strong><svg viewBox="0 0 72 104" aria-hidden="true"><g transform="translate(5 79)"><rect class="case" x="1" y="0" width="27" height="17" rx="1"/><path class="case-seam" d="M14.5 0v17M1 8.5h27"/><path class="pallet" d="M0 20h29M3 22v2m11.5-2v2M26 22v2"/></g><g transform="translate(38 79)"><rect class="case" x="1" y="0" width="27" height="17" rx="1"/><path class="case-seam" d="M14.5 0v17M1 8.5h27"/><path class="pallet" d="M0 20h29M3 22v2m11.5-2v2M26 22v2"/></g></svg><span>Week 4</span></div></div>
          <dl class="plan-costs">
            <div><dt>Purchase cost <span>400 cases × $25</span></dt><dd>$10,000</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Storage <span>20 pallet-weeks × $10</span></dt><dd>$200</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </section>
        <section class="buying-plan weekly" aria-labelledby="weekly-title">
          <h3 id="weekly-title">Buy one week at a time</h3>
          <p class="unit-price">$26 <span>per case</span></p>
          <p class="delivery-summary">100 cases in each of four deliveries</p>
          <p class="chart-heading">Pallets stored during each week</p>
          <div class="stock-chart" role="img" aria-label="Pallets held during weeks 1 to 4: 2, 2, 2, 2."><div class="stock-week"><strong>2</strong><svg viewBox="0 0 72 104" aria-hidden="true"><g transform="translate(5 79)"><rect class="case" x="1" y="0" width="27" height="17" rx="1"/><path class="case-seam" d="M14.5 0v17M1 8.5h27"/><path class="pallet" d="M0 20h29M3 22v2m11.5-2v2M26 22v2"/></g><g transform="translate(38 79)"><rect class="case" x="1" y="0" width="27" height="17" rx="1"/><path class="case-seam" d="M14.5 0v17M1 8.5h27"/><path class="pallet" d="M0 20h29M3 22v2m11.5-2v2M26 22v2"/></g></svg><span>Week 1</span></div><div class="stock-week"><strong>2</strong><svg viewBox="0 0 72 104" aria-hidden="true"><g transform="translate(5 79)"><rect class="case" x="1" y="0" width="27" height="17" rx="1"/><path class="case-seam" d="M14.5 0v17M1 8.5h27"/><path class="pallet" d="M0 20h29M3 22v2m11.5-2v2M26 22v2"/></g><g transform="translate(38 79)"><rect class="case" x="1" y="0" width="27" height="17" rx="1"/><path class="case-seam" d="M14.5 0v17M1 8.5h27"/><path class="pallet" d="M0 20h29M3 22v2m11.5-2v2M26 22v2"/></g></svg><span>Week 2</span></div><div class="stock-week"><strong>2</strong><svg viewBox="0 0 72 104" aria-hidden="true"><g transform="translate(5 79)"><rect class="case" x="1" y="0" width="27" height="17" rx="1"/><path class="case-seam" d="M14.5 0v17M1 8.5h27"/><path class="pallet" d="M0 20h29M3 22v2m11.5-2v2M26 22v2"/></g><g transform="translate(38 79)"><rect class="case" x="1" y="0" width="27" height="17" rx="1"/><path class="case-seam" d="M14.5 0v17M1 8.5h27"/><path class="pallet" d="M0 20h29M3 22v2m11.5-2v2M26 22v2"/></g></svg><span>Week 3</span></div><div class="stock-week"><strong>2</strong><svg viewBox="0 0 72 104" aria-hidden="true"><g transform="translate(5 79)"><rect class="case" x="1" y="0" width="27" height="17" rx="1"/><path class="case-seam" d="M14.5 0v17M1 8.5h27"/><path class="pallet" d="M0 20h29M3 22v2m11.5-2v2M26 22v2"/></g><g transform="translate(38 79)"><rect class="case" x="1" y="0" width="27" height="17" rx="1"/><path class="case-seam" d="M14.5 0v17M1 8.5h27"/><path class="pallet" d="M0 20h29M3 22v2m11.5-2v2M26 22v2"/></g></svg><span>Week 4</span></div></div>
          <dl class="plan-costs">
            <div><dt>Purchase cost <span>400 cases × $26</span></dt><dd>$10,400</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Storage <span>8 pallet-weeks × $10</span></dt><dd>$80</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </section>
      </div>
      <p class="movement-note">50 cases per pallet. Deliveries arrive at the start of each week; 100 cases leave at the end. Each pictured pallet represents one pallet held for that week.</p>

      <div class="tradeoff">
        <div class="tradeoff-math"><p><strong>$400</strong><span>saved on the goods</span></p><span class="operator" aria-label="minus">−</span><p><strong>$120</strong><span>extra storage</span></p></div>
        <div class="remaining"><span class="remaining-value">$280</span><p>left to cover financing<br>and any other differences</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="lesson">The discount gives you a reason to consider holding stock. The next question is whether funding it—and using the money here—is worth that remaining $280.</p>

      <section class="payment-section" aria-labelledby="payment-title">
        <h3 id="payment-title">Could the same stock work with different terms?</h3>
        <p>Keep the 400-case delivery and its $25 rate. Change only the agreed date for paying its $10,000 invoice.</p>
        <fieldset class="payment-controls">
          <legend>When do you pay for the bulk order?</legend>
          <div class="choices">
            <label><input type="radio" name="payment-terms" id="terms-delivery" value="delivery" checked><span>On delivery</span></label>
            <label><input type="radio" name="payment-terms" id="terms-30" value="30"><span>Agreed 30-day terms</span></label>
          </div>
        </fieldset>
        <div class="payment-result" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
          <p class="scenario delivery"><strong>$10,000 leaves on day 0.</strong> You have paid for all four weeks of stock before any customer payment arrives.</p>
          <p class="scenario credit"><strong>$10,000 leaves on day 30.</strong> All the stock has shipped by day 28. You pay later, while the same $200 storage bill remains.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="payment-facts">
          <p><span>Customer payment dates</span><strong>Days 37, 44, 51 and 58</strong><small>Each weekly shipment is paid 30 days after dispatch.</small></p>
          <p><span>What the change affects</span><strong>Time spent funding the purchase</strong><small>The price, stock movement and storage charge stay the same.</small></p>
        </div>
        <details class="payment-detail"><summary>Compare the supplier payment schedules</summary>
          <div class="schedule-wrap"><table><caption>Days measured from the first delivery</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Buying arrangement</th><th scope="col">Supplier payments</th></tr></thead><tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">Four weeks at once</th><td><span class="scenario delivery">$10,000 on day 0</span><span class="scenario credit">$10,000 on day 30</span></td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Weekly deliveries, paid on arrival</th><td>$2,600 on days 0, 7, 14 and 21</td></tr>
          </tbody></table></div>
          <p>Customer payments arrive in stages, so the amount needing funding changes over time. These dates alone do not give a financing cost.</p>
        </details>
      </section>
      <figcaption id="example-assumptions"><strong>Illustrative example, in USD.</strong> Substitute your own purchase prices and storage costs. Demand is assumed to be steady, weekly supply reliable and shelf life sufficient for the plan and customers’ requirements.</figcaption>
      <details class="assumptions-detail"><summary>What still needs checking before choosing?</summary><p>The $280 is a difference after purchase and storage costs, not profit. Compare financing, the alternative uses of the cash, and any differences in freight, handling, waste or service. Confirm actual lead times and demand; no safety stock is modelled here. The later payment date is an agreed term, with the bulk price unchanged.</p></details>
    </figure>
